> Module Standard_deduction

# Standard deduction (Form 1040 line 12)

Direct File module `standardDeduction.xml`. Issue #11. Tests are in
`catala/tests/test_standard_deduction.catala_en`.

> Using Types
> Using Params_2024 as P

Inputs follow `catala/CONVENTIONS.md`: filing status, the age and blindness
flags, and the dependent-filer flag are plain inputs here. They are computed
by the filers and household modules (#15 to #20), which take the Direct File
facts named in the comment on each input. The one exception is the age test
itself (section "Age 65 and the day before the birthday"), which is a small
self-contained scope so the day-before-birthday rule can be tested.

## 26 U.S.C. § 63(c) Standard deduction

### (1) In general

"Except as otherwise provided in this subsection, the term "standard
deduction" means the sum of— (A) the basic standard deduction, and (B) the
additional standard deduction." (`sources/statute/irc-63.html`)

### (2) Basic standard deduction

"(A) 200 percent of the dollar amount in effect under subparagraph (C) for the
taxable year in the case of— (i) a joint return, or (ii) a surviving spouse
(as defined in section 2(a)), (B) $4,400 in the case of a head of household
(as defined in section 2(b)), or (C) $3,000 in any other case." For taxable
years 2018 to 2025, § 63(c)(7) substitutes $18,000 and $12,000 and § 63(c)(4)
indexes them. The TY2024 results are in Rev. Proc. 2023-34 § 3.15(1)
(`sources/revproc/rp-23-34.pdf` p 12) and are the `Params_2024` constants
`std_deduction_*`.

Direct File: `/singleOrMFSStandardDeduction` (14,600), `/MFJStandardDeduction`
(29,200), `/HoHStandardDeduction` (21,900) and `/filingStatusStandardDeduction`,
which gives MFJ and QSS the joint amount, Single and MFS the unmarried amount
and HoH the head-of-household amount.

### (3) Additional standard deduction for aged and blind

"the additional standard deduction is the sum of each additional amount to
which the taxpayer is entitled under subsection (f)."

### (5) Limitation on basic standard deduction in the case of certain dependents

"In the case of an individual with respect to whom a deduction under section
151 is allowable to another taxpayer ..., the basic standard deduction
applicable to such individual ... shall not exceed the greater of— (A) $500,
or (B) the sum of $250 and such individual's earned income." Indexed for 2024
to $1,300 and $450 (Rev. Proc. 2023-34 § 3.15(2), `rp-23-34.pdf` p 12).

### (6) Certain individuals, etc., not eligible for standard deduction

"(A) a married individual filing a separate return where either spouse
itemizes deductions, (B) a nonresident alien individual, ... the standard
deduction shall be zero." Direct File does not model these cases: itemizing is
out of scope (issue #11 "Out of scope") and nonresident aliens are knocked
out elsewhere. Not modelled here.

## 26 U.S.C. § 63(f) Aged or blind additional amounts

"(1) The taxpayer shall be entitled to an additional amount of $600— (A) for
himself if he has attained age 65 before the close of his taxable year, and
(B) for the spouse of the taxpayer if the spouse has attained age 65 before
the close of the taxable year and an additional exemption is allowable to the
taxpayer for such spouse under section 151(b). (2) ... for blind ... (3) In
the case of an individual who is not married and is not a surviving spouse,
paragraphs (1) and (2) shall be applied by substituting "$750" for "$600"."
The 2024 amounts are $1,550 and $1,950 (Rev. Proc. 2023-34 § 3.15(3),
`rp-23-34.pdf` p 12; Form 1040 instructions `i1040gi--2024.pdf` p 34).

"if the spouse dies during the taxable year the determination of whether such
spouse is blind shall be made as of the time of such death."

### Age 65 and the day before the birthday

Pub. 501 and the Form 1040 instructions treat a person as age 65 at the end of
the year if the 65th birthday is on or before January 1 of the next year
(`sources/pubs`, Pub. 501; Direct File `/filers/*/age65OrOlder` description,
`filers.xml` line 648). Direct File implements this by counting the birthday
as the day before the date of birth (`/filers/*/dayBeforeDateOfBirth`,
`filers.xml` line 357): a person born on January 1, 1960 turns 65 on
December 31, 2024 and gets the extra amount.

For a spouse who died in the year, the age is the age on the date of death,
again with the day before the birthday as the birthday
(`/secondaryFilerAgeDayBeforeDeath`, `filers.xml` line 3457;
`/MFJDeceasedSpouseReachedAge65ForStandardD`, line 3659).

```catala-metadata
declaration scope Age65DayBeforeBirthday:
  # Inputs: the birth date and the date at which age is measured
  # (December 31 of the tax year for a living filer, the date of death for a
  # deceased spouse).
  input date_of_birth content date
  input as_of content date
  # DF: filers.xml /filers/*/dayBeforeDateOfBirth
  internal day_before_birthday content date
  # DF: filers.xml /filers/*/ageCalculatedDayBeforeDOB (living filer) and
  # /secondaryFilerAgeDayBeforeDeath (deceased spouse): completed years
  # from the day before the date of birth to `as_of`.
  output age content integer
  # DF: filers.xml /filers/*/age65OrOlder and
  # /MFJDeceasedSpouseReachedAge65ForStandardD
  output is_65_or_older condition
```

```catala
scope Age65DayBeforeBirthday:
  definition day_before_birthday equals date_of_birth - 1 day
  definition age equals
    (Date.get_year of as_of - Date.get_year of day_before_birthday) -
    (if (Date.get_month of as_of < Date.get_month of day_before_birthday)
        or (Date.get_month of as_of = Date.get_month of day_before_birthday
            and Date.get_day of as_of < Date.get_day of day_before_birthday)
     then 1 else 0)
  rule is_65_or_older under condition age >= 65 consequence fulfilled
```

## Standard deduction scope

Direct File facts, in order: `/filerMFSAndSpouseIsEligibleForStandardDeductions`,
`/isSpouseInfoApplicableForStandardDeductions`,
`/secondaryFilerIs65OrOlderForDeduction`,
`/secondaryFilerAdditionalStandardDeductionItems`, `/isSpouse65OrOlder`,
`/additionalStandardDeductionItems`, `/additionalStandardDeductionMultiplier`,
`/additionalStandardDeduction`, `/filingStatusStandardDeduction`,
`/normalStandardDeduction`, `/minimumStandardDeduction`, `/standardDeduction`.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope StandardDeduction:
  # DF: filingStatus.xml /filingStatus (Writable)
  input filing_status content Types.FilingStatus
  # DF: filingStatus.xml /treatAsMFS
  input treat_as_mfs condition
  # DF: filers.xml /primaryFiler/isBlind
  input primary_filer_is_blind condition
  # DF: filers.xml /primaryFiler/age65OrOlder
  input primary_filer_age65_or_older condition
  # DF: filers.xml /secondaryFiler/isBlind
  input secondary_filer_is_blind condition
  # DF: filers.xml /secondaryFiler/age65OrOlder
  input secondary_filer_age65_or_older condition
  # DF: filers.xml /isWidowedInTaxYear
  input is_widowed_in_tax_year condition
  # DF: filers.xml /MFJDeceasedSpouseReachedAge65ForStandardD
  input mfj_deceased_spouse_reached_age65 condition
  # DF: filers.xml /MFSSpouse65OrOlder (Writable)
  input mfs_spouse_65_or_older condition
  # DF: filers.xml /MFSSpouseProvidesNoBenefits
  input mfs_spouse_provides_no_benefits condition
  # DF: filers.xml /treatFilersAsDependents
  input treat_filers_as_dependents condition
  # DF: income.xml /employerIncomeSubtotal (earned income for the
  # dependent minimum)
  input employer_income_subtotal content money

  # DF: standardDeduction.xml /filerMFSAndSpouseIsEligibleForStandardDeductions
  internal filer_mfs_and_spouse_is_eligible_for_standard_deductions condition
  # DF: /isSpouseInfoApplicableForStandardDeductions
  output is_spouse_info_applicable_for_standard_deductions condition
  # DF: /secondaryFilerIs65OrOlderForDeduction
  internal secondary_filer_is_65_or_older_for_deduction condition
  # DF: /secondaryFilerAdditionalStandardDeductionItems
  internal secondary_filer_additional_standard_deduction_items content integer
  # DF: /isSpouse65OrOlder (Form 1040 Spouse65OrOlderInd)
  output is_spouse_65_or_older condition
  # DF: /additionalStandardDeductionItems
  output additional_standard_deduction_items content integer
  # DF: /additionalStandardDeductionMultiplier
  internal additional_standard_deduction_multiplier content money
  # DF: /additionalStandardDeduction
  internal additional_standard_deduction content money
  # DF: /filingStatusStandardDeduction
  internal filing_status_standard_deduction content money
  # DF: /normalStandardDeduction
  internal normal_standard_deduction content money
  # DF: /minimumStandardDeduction
  internal minimum_standard_deduction content money
  # DF: /standardDeduction; Form 1040 line 12
  output standard_deduction content money
```

### Whose age and blindness count

"for the spouse of the taxpayer if the spouse has attained age 65 ..." (§ 63(f)(1)(B)).
Direct File counts the second filer's items only for MFJ, or for MFS when the
spouse is eligible for a standard deduction (the spouse files no return, has
no gross income and cannot be claimed as a dependent). This is Pub. 501's rule
that a married person filing separately may claim the spouse's additional
amount only if the spouse has no gross income, is not filing a return and
cannot be claimed as a dependent.

```catala
scope StandardDeduction:
  # DF: /filerMFSAndSpouseIsEligibleForStandardDeductions
  definition filer_mfs_and_spouse_is_eligible_for_standard_deductions equals
    treat_as_mfs and not mfs_spouse_provides_no_benefits

  # DF: /isSpouseInfoApplicableForStandardDeductions
  definition is_spouse_info_applicable_for_standard_deductions equals
    filing_status = MarriedFilingJointly
    or filer_mfs_and_spouse_is_eligible_for_standard_deductions

  # DF: /secondaryFilerIs65OrOlderForDeduction. For MFJ with a spouse who
  # died in the year the age at death is used (the input already is).
  definition secondary_filer_is_65_or_older_for_deduction equals
    if filing_status = MarriedFilingJointly and is_widowed_in_tax_year
    then mfj_deceased_spouse_reached_age65
    else if filing_status = MarriedFilingSeparately
    then mfs_spouse_65_or_older
    else (not (filing_status = HeadOfHousehold))
         and secondary_filer_age65_or_older

  # DF: /secondaryFilerAdditionalStandardDeductionItems
  definition secondary_filer_additional_standard_deduction_items equals
    if is_spouse_info_applicable_for_standard_deductions then
      (if secondary_filer_is_blind then 1 else 0) +
      (if secondary_filer_is_65_or_older_for_deduction then 1 else 0)
    else 0

  # DF: /isSpouse65OrOlder
  rule is_spouse_65_or_older
    under condition is_spouse_info_applicable_for_standard_deductions
                    and secondary_filer_is_65_or_older_for_deduction
    consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /additionalStandardDeductionItems (primary: blind, 65 or older)
  definition additional_standard_deduction_items equals
    (if primary_filer_is_blind then 1 else 0) +
    (if primary_filer_age65_or_older then 1 else 0) +
    secondary_filer_additional_standard_deduction_items
```

### Amounts

```catala
scope StandardDeduction:
  # Rev. Proc. 2023-34 §3.15(3). DF: /additionalStandardDeductionMultiplier
  definition additional_standard_deduction_multiplier equals
    match filing_status with pattern
    -- Single : P.std_deduction_additional_unmarried
    -- HeadOfHousehold : P.std_deduction_additional_unmarried
    -- MarriedFilingJointly : P.std_deduction_additional_married
    -- QualifyingSurvivingSpouse : P.std_deduction_additional_married
    -- MarriedFilingSeparately : P.std_deduction_additional_married

  # IRC 63(c)(3). DF: /additionalStandardDeduction
  definition additional_standard_deduction equals
    additional_standard_deduction_multiplier *
    (decimal of additional_standard_deduction_items)

  # IRC 63(c)(2). DF: /filingStatusStandardDeduction
  definition filing_status_standard_deduction equals
    match filing_status with pattern
    -- Single : P.std_deduction_unmarried
    -- MarriedFilingSeparately : P.std_deduction_married_separate
    -- HeadOfHousehold : P.std_deduction_head_of_household
    -- MarriedFilingJointly : P.std_deduction_joint_or_surviving_spouse
    -- QualifyingSurvivingSpouse : P.std_deduction_joint_or_surviving_spouse

  # IRC 63(c)(1). DF: /normalStandardDeduction
  definition normal_standard_deduction equals
    filing_status_standard_deduction + additional_standard_deduction
```

### Filers who can be claimed as a dependent

The dependent limit of § 63(c)(5) applies to the *basic* standard deduction.
Direct File adds the additional amount inside the minimum instead, so the
minimum is `GreaterOf($1,300, earned + $450) + additional`, and the result is
the lesser of the minimum and the normal amount. This is the arithmetic of the
Pub. 501 "Standard Deduction Worksheet for Dependents" (the greater of $1,300
or earned income plus $450, capped at the basic amount, then the additional
amounts are added), because
`min(max(1300, e+450) + add, basic + add) = min(max(1300, e+450), basic) + add`.

```catala
scope StandardDeduction:
  # IRC 63(c)(5), Rev. Proc. 2023-34 §3.15(2). DF: /minimumStandardDeduction
  definition minimum_standard_deduction equals
    (Money.max of P.std_deduction_dependent_floor,
       (employer_income_subtotal + P.std_deduction_dependent_earned_income_addition))
    + additional_standard_deduction

  # Form 1040 line 12. DF: /standardDeduction
  definition standard_deduction equals
    if treat_filers_as_dependents
    then Money.min of minimum_standard_deduction, normal_standard_deduction
    else normal_standard_deduction
```
